ewest usable poll is 78 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Open seat: Ashley Hinson (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Iowa's 2nd District is an open-seat contest after Republican Ashley Hinson left the seat to run for Senate. The district leans Republican by about four points, but the national environment favors Democrats this cycle, and both parties view the seat as winnable. Republican Joe Mitchell and Democratic state Representative Lindsay James are running even in fundraising, with Mitchell holding a slight cash advantage while drawing far more outside opposition spending.\n\nExpert ratings are split: most call the race a Tossup, Inside Elections tilts Republican, Cook rates it Lean Republican, and two outlets rate it a Democratic flip. The only recent poll, from July and Democratic-sponsored, showed a one-point race. Prediction markets give the Democrat a modest edge. With thin and dated polling, this remains a genuine coin-flip leaning narrowly Democratic.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.5595, "margin": 0.94}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.5585, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6246, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.619, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.5799, "margin": 1.8}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.557, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6133, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6185, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.6098, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.5891, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.6068, "margin": 1.2}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.615, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.6272, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.559, "margin": 1.5}]}